Live presence via Supabase, and fix the counts workflow

The workflow failed once when a human push landed mid-scrape: its own push
was then rejected. It now pulls with rebase and retries three times. It also
commits crowd-history.json -- without it every run started from no history,
so the frozen-counter detection never fired.

Presence: an anonymous heartbeat every 20s, "here now" is distinct visitors
seen in the last 45s. RLS denies all direct table access; the only way in is
heartbeat() and the only way out is live_counts(), which returns aggregates.
Verified the publishable key cannot read rows (empty set) or insert them (401).

badge.js is the one-liner makers embed so their own count becomes measured
rather than scraped.

